{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 8386c58b, NF-2: yes. The accepted install result\ncarries `phase: \"accepted\"`, taken from `kept.record.phase`. The word\n`recorded` goes.\n\nWhy. `phase` in an act result says where this client's kept request\nstands, and `recorded` is not one of the eight custody words. The\nchange does not reach the command line. The renderer reads `phase`\nonly for `application_installation`, and for an install request it\nprints `answer`, `reason` and `item`. So the output of `dap` stays\nequal, and ruling 84f4aa13 holds.\n\nConditions.\n1. The `next` sentence stays. It still says that installation can be\n   pending or refused after the request is accepted.\n2. `application_installation` is a read, not an act result. It keeps\n   `state` and its own `phase`, which is the phase of the installation.\n   If its description does not say that, make it say so.\n3. The head note lists this change among the result changes, with the\n   host-none witness as you wrote it.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}